Experiment No.: 15

Title

Interfacing Servo Motor with Arduino

Aim

To control a servo motor using Arduino.

Theory

A servo motor is an actuator that provides precise angular movement. Arduino controls the servo position using PWM signals.

Components Required
Arduino Uno
Servo Motor
Jumper Wires
Procedure
Connect servo signal pin to Arduino pin 9.
Connect power and ground pins.
Include Servo library.
Upload the program.
Observe servo rotation.
Code
#include <Servo.h>

Servo myServo;

void setup()
{
  myServo.attach(9);
}

void loop()
{
  myServo.write(0);
  delay(1000);

  myServo.write(90);
  delay(1000);

  myServo.write(180);
  delay(1000);
}
Output

Servo rotates to 0°, 90°, and 180° positions.

Result

Servo motor was successfully interfaced with Arduino.

Conclusion

The control of servo motor using Arduino was studied successfully.
